      {
        "id": 38342,
        "name": "Cosmonaut Zero",
        "username": "Cosmonaut_Zero",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/cosmonaut_zero/{size}/2520_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-09-13T18:44:13.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"McBehrer\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mcbehrer/48/1850_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> McBehrer:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Except, you switched your trash with your deck, so what WAS your trash is now your deck. THEN you shuffle your deck. So no, you can't order your cards that way. Nice try though.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Yep. That's exactly what I said. No sorted Nightmist decks because you have to shuffle. Even if you're not normally allowed to sort your trash (which I kinda do anyway for convenience with some Heroes/Villains), Nightmist would then be able to choose the order in which the cards that used to be her deck entered her trash under the interpretation that your trash is always considered to be a collection of individual cards and never a unit in itself, effectively ordering it as she wished. You'd end up with a shuffled deck and a sorted trash. Not sure why exactly she'd care to do so or why it would matter, but it would be a thing that could happen I guess.</p>",
        "post_number": 21,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:12:06.778Z",
