        "id": 38343,
        "name": "Rabit",
        "username": "Rabit",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/{size}/7330_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-09-13T19:34:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"robalan\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/9fc348/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> robalan:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Slightly off topic, but… am I the only one who usually orders their Trash?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Nope.  <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/sunglasses.png?v=12\" title=\":sunglasses:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":sunglasses:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<p>Yeah, not so much with Tachy (I use a spindown d20 for tracking bursts), but definitely in other situations, including Unity&nbsp;and her bots (to find later), Argent Adept and his Instruments, and Expatriette and her Ammo. Often I'll just have the cards I care about rotated 90 degrees&nbsp;for easy access, but the idea's the same.</p>",
