      {
        "id": 38346,
        "name": "Envisioner",
        "username": "Envisioner",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-10-15T06:43:13.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"phantaskippy\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/48/1897_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> phantaskippy:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>As many times as I've played Visionary, I have never used Brain Burn.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>It's usually a dead card, but can prevent game loss against Terralunar Blade (esp. on Advanced), makes a great turn-1 play against the Chairman, counteracts Forced Deployment as very little else can, and can reduce the hassle of dealing with Omnitron, Citizen Dawn, and so forth, so it has lots of potential applications, though all of them pretty niche and only a few really worth the damage you take.&nbsp; (If only you could Wrest yourself…)&nbsp; Usually I'll discard it to Enlighten, but not always.&nbsp; I do wish it was a singleton.</p>\n<p>In the case of the Matriarch, however, its usefulness varies extremely drastically based on whether you can stack or not; other villains care only a little, but with Matty, whether you choose the order means the difference between just buying 1-2 turns before she flips, or foiling a Darken the Skies that you know is coming up, versus being able to completely and utterly make one of the game's only diff-4 villains your b****.&nbsp; (For this reason, I find myself wanting to rule that you should shuffle the trash first, and put it under the deck without looking at the bottom card.&nbsp; I will probably play this way in future, now that I've beaten the Matriarch once and proven that it can be done…it wasn't as lame as when I steamrolled the Dreamer, but it was still a rather sad and pathetic end for this, well, sad and pathetic but nonetheless REALLY POWERFUL villainess.)</p>",
        "post_number": 25,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:12:07.080Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
