      {
        "id": 38348,
        "name": "Envisioner",
        "username": "Envisioner",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-11-13T04:43:22.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>This question came up again tonight, and the answer was <em>really</em> important in this case.&nbsp; Going up against La Capitan, I have La Paradoja, The Infuriating Mable, Final Breath, and Raiding Party in the trash, along with Plunder.&nbsp; I really want to put the ship on the very bottom, with Raiding Party under it and Mable atop it, with Final Breath atop that and Plunder on top.&nbsp; If I'm not allowed to reorder the trash when Brain Burning (which, for the sake of fairness, I will currently assume), then I still get to put Plunder on top, but Raiding Party is second, and will bring out Mable and Final Breath, and Raiding Party and Mable will both destroy O/Es that turn, and Cappy will be two turns closer to getting to reshuffle her deck and resume being horrifying.&nbsp; True, this is all 14 turns away, but I take nothing for granted when fighting Maria Helena Etc. Etc.&nbsp; I really wish Christopher would confirm whether we're allowed to stack or not - if we are, The Matriarch is taken down a notch and that'd be sad, but if we aren't, it contributes to the general issue of La Capitan being far, far too tough for her printed difficulty of 2, taking away one of the better strategies for dealing with her.</p>",
        "post_number": 26,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:12:07.156Z",
