      {
        "id": 38349,
        "name": "McBehrer",
        "username": "McBehrer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mcbehrer/{size}/1850_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-11-13T18:10:38.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Well, the cards will SAY whether you need to shuffle or not. Any time you have seen the order of the cards (like from a search or reveal) you HAVE to shuffle your deck, unless the main benefit of the card WAS to see the order of the cards. Brain Burn lets you put the trash (which you are explicitly allowed to look through at any time) and move all the cards from it (individually, not as a group) back to the bottom of the deck. It doesn't SAY to shuffle, so it would appear that the omission was intentional, by my reasoning.</p>",
        "post_number": 27,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:12:07.219Z",
