      {
        "id": 38353,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-11-14T18:04:06.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>We used Brain Burn to stop the The Matriarch from flipping, since it refills the deck without shuffling the trash in.</p><p>Stealth Bot was valiant in her sacrifice.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>This is how I view this card and how you would sort the deck.</p><p>1. &nbsp;There is no rule stopping you from re-ordering the villain trash.</p><p>2. &nbsp;Brain burn has you put the trash on the bottom of the deck.</p><p>3. &nbsp;Even if Brain Burn did not allow reordering, you could reorder the villain trash directly before playing Brain Burn, then just put it under the deck.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>So basically even if the card doesn't allow you to stack the deck, you can still do it, since you can stack the trash right before playing the card.</p><p>Unless we get a ruling that trash order cannot be alterred by players this will be an option, with the amount of cards that shuffle the trash before revealling I don't expect that ruling to ever be made.</p>",
        "post_number": 29,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:12:07.375Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
