      {
        "id": 38356,
        "name": "Slamin",
        "username": "Slamin",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/bcef8e/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-05-16T03:45:55.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Envisioner\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Envisioner:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>We do have at least one case where trash order needs to be preserved: Lost in the Past.&nbsp; If there's anything that shuffles the Environment trash, that messes with Silver Gulch in a big way.&nbsp; But yes, villains shuffle their trash often enough that an effect requiring villain decks to preserve trash order is unlikely to ever exist, unless some new villain deck itself contains that as a gimmick.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I don't have Silver Gluch so I don't have any reference for Lost in the Past. &nbsp;I would like to see a ruling about intentionally reordering the villian trash. &nbsp;Shuffling the villian trash makes sense if required of course but I don't see why people feel that because reordering isn't explicitly disallowed in the rules that it is okay. &nbsp;I don't remembering seeing a rule about reordering the villian deck anywhere either. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/wink.png?v=12\" title=\":wink:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":wink:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>",
        "post_number": 31,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:12:07.532Z",
